/* Modern theme for the login dialog -- fully programmatic, flat colors/vector shapes instead of
   legacy art.

   Reference construction for a modern-theme dialog, built from explicit RML layers (base.rcss's
   forged-dialog primitives) PLUS real box-shadow. Real box-shadow (inset and outset, genuine blur,
   comma-separated multiple shadows) IS supported by this vendored renderer as of the SDL_GPU
   backend's PR-989 integration -- confirmed by reading the actual source (PropertyParserBoxShadow/
   GeometryBoxShadow/RmlUi_Renderer_SDL_GPU.cpp), not assumed; see base.rcss's own header comment
   for the full trace. Shadow/depth is real box-shadow directly on the element it belongs to (no
   shadow-plane divs), so the shell reads as outer iron edge -> window surface -> inner groove.

   One conversion gotcha carried through every box-shadow value below: this engine's rgba() parses
   alpha via a 0-255 integer (atoi), NOT a 0-1 CSS float -- the browser reference's
   `rgba(0,0,0,.62)` would parse as alpha 0 (invisible) if copied verbatim. Every color below is
   pre-converted to the 0-255 form (e.g. .62 -> 158).

   No ::before/::after, `content:`, or percentage border-radius anywhere. The hero-plate ornaments
   AND the checkbox checkmark use a real `transform: rotate(45deg)`/`rotate(-45deg)` element --
   SetTransform is genuinely wired into this renderer's vertex stage (verified against source:
   RmlUi_Renderer_SDL_GPU.cpp's Matrix4f/vertex-uniform path). The checkmark previously used a
   5-div pixel-stacked stand-in from before rotate() was confirmed reliable; it's now the
   reference's own single rotated border-corner technique. */

body {
	width: 100%;
	height: 100%;
	margin: 0;
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* Window surface. Crimson belongs to the hero banner ONLY -- #panel uses plain .modern-frame
   (no -crimson variant), and background-color/decorator are overridden directly here to the
   reference's own neutral forged-window fill, replacing .modern-frame's own semi-transparent
   olive-leaning default. Border is a single flat tone (reference: `1px solid #46463b`), not a
   bevel -- real box-shadow now carries the surface's entire depth read (broad soft drop shadow,
   dense contact shadow, a dark inner hairline, a warm inner band) instead of a per-side
   border-color trick.

   This is the visible "frame" strip between the exterior shell-edge (-3dp) and the inner groove
   (+4dp) -- it needs to read as a distinctly LIGHTER metal band than the recessed content well
   inside the groove, WITHOUT that light leaking further inward. The reference's own literal
   top-of-gradient stop (`#11130f`) and box-shadow alpha (`.18` = 46/255) produce that contrast
   fine in a browser, but rendered over an actual 3D game scene in this engine both read as
   near-invisible. First attempt brightened the decorator's own top stop -- wrong tool: decorator
   paints across #panel's ENTIRE box, not just the 4dp ring, and .login-groove/the area around
   .login-hero-banner have no opaque fill of their own there, so the brightened top-of-gradient
   showed straight through into the "recessed" interior instead of staying confined to the frame.
   Reverted the decorator to its original dark values -- the box-shadow inset band below is
   inherently confined to exactly 3dp from the border (fixed spread, no blur), so THAT'S the right
   place to push contrast: alpha raised to 190/255 (was 46, then 100) with no decorator change. */
#panel {
    position: absolute;
    width: 329dp;
    height: 245dp;

    font-family: "token(font-body)";
    font-size: 12dp;
    color: token(text-primary);

    border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;

    background-color: #080a08;
    decorator:
        linear-gradient(to bottom, #11130f 0%, #080a08 100%);

    border-width: 1dp;
    border-color: token(border-frame);

    box-shadow:
        0 11dp 30dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 158),
        0 2dp 5dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 217),
        inset 0 0 0 1dp #090a08,
        inset 0 0 0 3dp rgba(90, 87, 69, 46);
}

/* Outer iron edge, -3dp. Transparent fill -- the reference's own exterior layer has NO background,
   only a border + inset lighting; a solid metal-outer fill here was turning this into a second
   opaque rectangle behind the window surface instead of a thin edge. Border is a single flat tone
   (reference: `1px solid rgba(31,31,26,.95)`); the asymmetric per-edge lighting the reference
   expresses as 4 separate inset box-shadows is reproduced directly here instead of folding it into
   border-*-color, boosted the same way and for the same reason as #panel's own band above. */
.login-shell-edge {
    background-color: transparent;
    border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
    border-color: rgba(31, 31, 26, 242);

    box-shadow:
        inset 1dp 0 0 rgba(130, 121, 91, 28),
        inset -1dp 0 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 204),
        inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(151, 139, 101, 20),
        inset 0 -1dp 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 230);
}

/* Inner groove, ~4dp inward -- flat border tone matching the reference's own
   `inset: 4px; border: 1px solid #24261f`, PLUS the two inset shadows the reference also carries
   here (`inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(121,112,83,.06), inset 0 0 12px rgba(0,0,0,.6)`) -- a thin warm
   hairline catch plus a broad 12dp inward darkness. That broad darkness is what makes the
   perimeter actually read as recessed/carved into the shell; the border alone was too thin an
   effect on its own. */
.login-groove {
    position: absolute;

    left: 4dp;
    right: 4dp;
    top: 4dp;
    bottom: 4dp;

    pointer-events: none;

    border-width: 1dp;
    border-color: #24261f;

    box-shadow:
        inset 0 0 0 1dp rgba(121, 112, 83, 15),
        inset 0 0 12dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 153);
}

/* The hero-banner IS Login's header -- it spans the same footprint the (now-removed) separate
   iron rail used to occupy. This is deliberately NOT nested inside a metal rail: the reference
   treats .window__header (metal, one center rivet) and .hero-banner (crimson, two side rivets)
   as alternative header styles for different windows, never combined into one composite. Depth
   (inset highlight/seat + cast shadow) comes from base.rcss's .modern-title-plate box-shadow. */
.login-hero-banner {
	left: 8dp;
	right: 8dp;
	top: 8dp;
	height: 37dp;
}

/* Ornaments are diamonds INSIDE the plate now (left/right:8dp from the plate's own edges,
   matching the reference), not external end-caps -- a real 11x11 square rotated 45deg (apparent
   ~15.6dp). Previously these were narrow external stacked blocks that read as brackets, not
   diamonds/studs. */
.login-hero-cap {
	position: absolute;
	top: 50%;
	width: 11dp;
	height: 11dp;
	margin-top: -5.5dp;
	background-color: #24100a;
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: #6a2a19;
	transform: rotate(45deg);
	pointer-events: none;
	box-shadow:
		inset 1dp 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 145, 9),
		inset -1dp -1dp 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 173);
}
.login-hero-cap-left { left: 8dp; }
.login-hero-cap-right { right: 8dp; }

.label {
	position: absolute;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}

/* color/font-weight match the reference exactly (#e1b94e / 500) rather than the general-purpose
   token(text-warm)/bold. The reference centers via `inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center` --
   tried the flexbox equivalent (display:flex/align-items/justify-content) here since this engine
   has no CSS Grid, but a bare mustache-bound text node inside a flex container didn't render at
   all (RmlUi's flex layout apparently doesn't treat an anonymous/inline text child as a real flex
   item the way base.rcss's .tooltip__stat's actual ELEMENT children -- <strong>, etc. -- do).
   Reverted to plain absolute positioning + text-align, same mechanism as before, with top:11dp
   eyeballed to vertical-center a ~13dp line within the 37dp banner. letter-spacing is the
   reference's `.02em` converted to this font-size (13dp * 0.02 = 0.26dp), not the earlier
   unrelated 1.1px value. font-effect switches from `outline` to `shadow` -- the reference's own
   text-shadow is `0 1px 1px #000, 0 0 5px rgba(190,139,41,.10)`; `shadow(offset-x offset-y
   color)` reproduces the first (dominant) layer exactly (RmlUi's real font-effect, confirmed via
   FontEffectShadow.cpp's own property registration: offset-x, offset-y, color). The second, very
   subtle ambient glow (.10 alpha) is left unreproduced -- `glow()` exists on this engine too but
   needs 5 parameters (outline-width, blur-width, offset-x, offset-y, color) for a barely-visible
   effect, not worth the added complexity/risk here. */
.label-server {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 11dp;
	text-align: center;
	color: #e1b94e;
	font-family: "token(font-title)";
	font-size: 13dp;
	font-weight: 500;
	letter-spacing: 0.26dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}

/* Body is a real recessed cavity. top:50dp matches the reference's own `.login-body{top:50px}`
   exactly. (LoginWin.cpp::SetPosition() hardcodes the real CUITextInputBox overlay's Y offset as
   literal constants -- usernameY=72, passwordY=105 -- which happen to already line up with this
   value: 50dp local well top + input local top 16dp/49dp + a fixed 6dp text-padding baked into
   that C++ = 72/105 exactly. If that C++ offset is ever revisited, this is the value it's keyed
   to.) Broad inset recess shadow now comes from base.rcss's .modern-content-well box-shadow. */
.login-content {
	left: 9dp;
	right: 9dp;
	top: 50dp;
	height: 139dp;
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* Coordinates are local to .login-content, matching the reference's own .field-label exactly:
   color #8d835f (a muted brass tone, not the general-purpose token(text-secondary) gray), 8dp,
   weight 600, letter-spacing .08em (of 8dp = 0.64dp). Previously used token(text-secondary)/9dp/
   no letter-spacing/23dp+56dp top (2dp off the reference's own 25px/58px). */
.label-account {
	left: 21dp;
	top: 25dp;
	font-size: 8dp;
	font-weight: 600;
	letter-spacing: 0.64dp;
	color: #8d835f;
}
.label-password {
	left: 21dp;
	top: 58dp;
	font-size: 8dp;
	font-weight: 600;
	letter-spacing: 0.64dp;
	color: #8d835f;
}

.login-input {
	position: absolute;
	width: 156dp;
	height: 23dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
}
.login-input-account  { left: 100dp; top: 16dp; }
.login-input-password { left: 100dp; top: 49dp; }

.checkbox-row {
	position: absolute;
	cursor: pointer;
	pointer-events: auto;
}
.checkbox-remember-me   { left: 100dp; top: 84dp; }
.checkbox-save-password { left: 100dp; top: 108dp; }

/* The reference's checkbox has no per-instance bevel override on either checkbox-row -- it's one
   uniform look everywhere (base.rcss's .checkbox-box/.checkbox-box.checked). The previous
   top/left-corner bevel-catch overrides here (both unchecked and checked) were an earlier
   invented embellishment with no reference equivalent; removed.

   Checkmark is now the reference's own technique: a single 6x3 box with a left+bottom border,
   rotated -45deg, forming a check stroke -- not the previous 5-div pixel-stacked stand-in from
   before `rotate()` was confirmed reliable on this renderer. */
.checkbox-tick {
	display: none;
	position: absolute;
	left: 2dp;
	top: 1dp;
	width: 6dp;
	height: 3dp;
	border-left: 2dp #171006;
	border-bottom: 2dp #171006;
	transform: rotate(-45deg);
}
.checkbox-box.checked .checkbox-tick {
	display: block;
}

/* Footer is a structural container only -- see base.rcss's own .modern-footer-band comment. One
   plain border-top now carries the entire body-to-footer separation, matching the reference's own
   `.window__footer{border-top:1px solid #24251f;background:none}` exactly -- the previous
   shadow+shine two-line pair was more decorative than the reference. */
.login-footer {
	left: 9dp;
	right: 9dp;
	top: 190dp;
	height: 46dp;
	bottom: auto;
	pointer-events: none;
	border-top-width: 1dp;
	border-top-color: #24251f;
}

/* Position/size only -- color/box-shadow/font are now inherited from base.rcss's shared .btn/
   .btn-ok (promoted there once sys_menu became a second real consumer needing the identical
   reference values; this file used to carry a full private copy of all of it, which is exactly
   the kind of duplication that let sys_menu's own buttons silently stay on the old un-corrected
   look while Login's got fixed). */
.login-btn {
	top: 8dp;
	width: 76dp;
	height: 26dp;
	line-height: 26dp;
}

.login-btn-ok {
	left: 145dp;
}

.login-btn-cancel {
	left: 226dp;
}

.login-btn-label {
	position: relative;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}

/* Intentionally external to the forged dialog shell, as in the current UX. top:257dp matches the
   reference exactly (245dp window height + 12dp below it); font-effect/color/size match the
   reference's own `.trust-warning` (`color:#c99a3e;font-size:10px;text-shadow:0 1px 1px #000`). */
.trust-warning {
	position: absolute;
	left: 30dp;
	top: 257dp;
	width: 280dp;
	font-size: 10dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
	color: token(semantic-warning);
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}
